# .env.example — COMMITTED template of the variables this project needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE
#   1. cp .env.example .env        (setup.sh does this for you if .env is missing)
#   2. Fill REAL values in .env    — .env is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
#   3. Keep THIS file in sync       — when you add a var to .env, add a blank/placeholder
#                                     entry here so teammates and CI know it exists.
#
# RULES (enforced by guard.sh + the git pre-commit hook):
#   - Never put a real secret in this file. Placeholders only.
#   - The real .env stays out of git. Production secrets live in the host's own
#     settings (Vercel/Netlify dashboard, VPS env, secret manager) — not in any file.
#
# Onboarding tailors this to your real stack. The groups below are common examples —
# delete what you don't use, add what you do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- App ---------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=development
# APP_ENV=development
# PORT=3000
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- AI / agent keys (if the app itself calls models) ------------------------
# Do NOT confuse these with your Claude Code login — these are for the app's own
# runtime API calls, if any.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/dbname
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- Remote Postgres over SSH tunnel (scripts/pg-tunnel.ps1 + pg-mcp-register.ps1) --
# SSH hop (key auth, ~/.ssh/id_ed25519). Postgres itself is reached THROUGH the hop.
# PG_SSH_HOST=            # ip or hostname of the box that runs Postgres
# PG_SSH_USER=
# PG_SSH_PORT=22
# PG_LOCAL_PORT=5432      # local end of the tunnel; MCP connects here
# PG_REMOTE_HOST=127.0.0.1  # where Postgres listens AS SEEN FROM the SSH host
# PG_REMOTE_PORT=5432
# DB credentials on the remote machine (prefer a read-only role — see docs/pg-tunnel.md)
# PGUSER=
# PGPASSWORD=
# PGDATABASE=

# --- External services / APIs ------------------------------------------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Auth / sessions ---------------------------------------------------------
# AUTH_SECRET=
# JWT_SECRET=

# --- Deploy / infra (used by deploy skill; never the real values in git) ------
# DEPLOY_HOST=
# SSH_USER=
